From 650c163257151722648bab4bbc07bd1ba64909fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 13:55:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 49/51] begonia-wifi (fwport): drop dead UART/SDIO STP
 transports

The active STP transport on begonia is BTIF (live: sys_if_tx if=2, all tx via
mtk_wcn_btif_write). The UART(0) and SDIO(1) transports register if_tx callbacks
that are never selected on this SoC. Remove stp_uart.c, stp_sdio.c, hif_sdio.c
(~7.4K LOC) and resolve their callers:
 - wmt_dev / common_drv_init: drop the uart/sdio/hif drv_init/exit hooks
 - wmt_ctrl_sdio_func: no-op success (SDIO func-ctrl never taken on BTIF SoC),
   state-bit bookkeeping preserved
 - wmt_exp: drop the #if-0 SDIO chipid variant; live path is stub_alps (SoC chipid)
 - stp_exp: remove unreferenced exported mtk_wcn_stp_sdio_wake_up_ctrl wrapper
 - stp_dbg / stp_core: neuter COMBO/SDIO debug + helper wrappers (kept public API)
No register/BTIF/DMA/conn-MCU changes. SoC chip-id path unchanged. Boots clean,
wlan0 scans real APs. -146/+39 in edited files atop 3 file deletions.
